    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0792" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2091</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-05T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1915, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 6, 9 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2838. Chancellor and his friends seem very much afraid of Von Tirpitz and his press bureau. Friend who
                    occasionally gives me correct information says the Pope responsible for change
                    of German submarine policy; in return he is to work for peace which friend says
                    Germany now desires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
